## ⚠️ Required: Database Migration

The backend 500 errors (Weekly Targets + Notifications) are caused by **missing database table columns and tables**.

**Run this SQL on your `pt_lumora` MySQL database to fix it:**

```
c:\Kuliah\Semester_4\WEB-PROGRAMMING\Lumora\finpro-go\migrations\fix_schema.sql
```

**What it does:**
1. **Adds missing columns** to the `targets` table: `title`, `description`, `focus_dimension`, `priority`, `due_date`
2. **Changes `status` column** from ENUM(`active/completed/cancelled`) to VARCHAR so it supports `not_started/in_progress/completed`
3. **Creates `subtasks` table** if it doesn't exist (for target subtasks)
4. **Creates `notifications` table** if it doesn't exist (fixes the 500 on every page load)

### How to run:
Open your MySQL client and run:
```sql
SOURCE C:/Kuliah/Semester_4/WEB-PROGRAMMING/Lumora/finpro-go/migrations/fix_schema.sql;
```

Or using the MySQL CLI:
```bash
mysql -u root -p pt_lumora < finpro-go/migrations/fix_schema.sql
```

> [!IMPORTANT]
> After running the SQL, restart the Go server (`go run cmd/server/main.go`) to clear any cached connections.

